# AWS CCP — Management & Governance

Which service collects metrics and logs from your resources and raises alarms on them?
---
CloudWatch
= Amazon CloudWatch
---
An alarm can notify you or trigger an action like scaling out.

Which service records every API call in your account, answering who did what and when?
---
CloudTrail
= AWS CloudTrail
---
The audit log. CloudWatch is about performance, CloudTrail about actions.

Which service tracks how your resources are configured over time and checks them against rules?
---
Config
= AWS Config
---
CloudTrail says who made the change. Config shows the before and after, and flags drift.

Which service defines your infrastructure as code in JSON or YAML templates?
---
CloudFormation
= AWS CloudFormation
---
A stack is created, updated, and deleted as a unit. The CDK compiles real code down to it.

Which service manages your fleet at scale with patching, run commands, and a parameter store?
---
Systems Manager
= AWS Systems Manager
= SSM
---
Session Manager also gives shell access without opening SSH ports.

Which service shows AWS service outages and events that affect your specific account?
---
Health Dashboard
= AWS Health Dashboard
= AWS Health
= Personal Health Dashboard
---
The public status page for everyone, plus a personalized view for your resources.

Which service sets up and governs a secure multi-account environment with guardrails?
---
Control Tower
= AWS Control Tower
---
A landing zone built on Organizations. Guardrails are preconfigured SCPs and Config rules.

Which developer service automates the full release pipeline from source to deployment?
---
CodePipeline
~ CodeBuild
~ CodeDeploy
~ CloudFormation
---
CodeBuild compiles and tests, CodeDeploy pushes to targets, CodePipeline chains the stages.

Which service gives you a managed, browser-based shell with the AWS CLI preinstalled?
---
CloudShell
= AWS CloudShell
---
Free, already authenticated as you, and reachable from the console toolbar.
